Method poll returns result which is the element at head before removal. So assert that \result equals \old(this.get(0))? But get(0) returns element at index 0 before removal. However note that if queue empty, result null. In that case get(0) would likely throw IndexOutOfBoundsException, but maybe get defined to return element at index, might also throw if empty. But we can express: (\old(this.size()) > 0 => \result.equals(\old(this.get(0)))) && (\old(this.size()) == 0 => \result == null). Use old size. Need to use observers: size() method returns size, get(int) returns element at index. So we can write:

