analysisWe need to produce an assert statement for the comment after poll method.

We have comment: "@@@ The result of the method is equal to the value at the head of the queue before the method execution."

We need to express that \result equals the element that was at the head before execution. In priority queue, head is element at index 0 before poll. So we need to capture old value of queue[0] or using get(0) before execution. There is a public method get(int index) that returns element at index. So we can refer to \old(this.get(0)). Use \result == \old(this.get(0)). Since result is of type E, we can use equals? In spec they used equality for primitives and for objects they used .equals. In earlier examples they used this.contains(value) which returns boolean. For equality they used == for ints, but for objects they used .equals. For generic type E, we could use .equals. However they may accept == if they treat reference equality, but spec says equal to the value at head. Typically you want .equals. In previous examples they used this.query(i).equals(\old(this.query(i))) for object equality. So we should use .equals.

Thus assert \result.equals(\old(this.get(0))) ? But need to ensure \old(this.get(0)) is not null? The head could be null? The queue does not permit null elements, so it's non-null. So we can assert \result.equals(\old(this.get(0))) . But \result may be null if queue empty (result = null). In that case old head is null? Actually if empty, queue[0] is null, get(0) would probably throw IndexOutOfBoundsException. Wait get method likely checks bounds; but spec may not be required to handle empty case. The comment says "value at the head of the queue before the method execution". If queue empty, head value is undefined; result is null. Could express as (\old(this.size()) == 0 => \result == null) && (\old(this.size()) > 0 => \result.equals(\old(this.get(0)))) . That captures both cases.

Better to include both. Use size() method: this.size() returns current size after poll? Actually after poll, size decreased. So need old size: \old(this.size()). Use that.

Thus final assert:

assert (\old(this.size()) == 0 => \result == null) && (\old(this.size()) > 0 => \result.equals(\old(this.get(0))));

